why: reading the guide, the operator asked "then what IS app?" — and
  the guide does not say. The recipe-vs-running distinction lives in
  one cell of a comparison table; `Module.nothing` is not mentioned at
  all; and the typepedia, the reference people grep, has no entry for
  `Module`, `Fact` or `New`. Explanations that only exist in a chat
  are not documentation.

what: a short section saying what a Module IS (a value describing what
  to build; nothing runs until a region runs it; `app` is that value),
  `Module.nothing` named beside `contributing`, and typepedia entries
  for the DI vocabulary pointing at the guide.

